# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
# Not a song: the jingle a beaten boss gets (src/audio/fanfare.js plays it once, as a sound).
# Built on the title song (music/title.scrim): its knock and the thin ring held while time stands
# still (the end of its cracking), its shatter, and its toy tune, which lands this once on a major
# third (C#), with the glass bird's wide call after it.
title    Victory
composer Claude
about    A boss falls, and the bad memory loses its grip, like the title's glass bird: a knock and a thin glass ring while time stands still, then the shatter, wind chimes, and out of it the toy tune on crystal (A B C E D) over F and G, landing on an A major chord instead of minor, a crystal sweep rising, a singing bowl, and the bird's wide call ringing over it.
tempo    100
beats    2
steps    6
reverb   0.55

# mood explore: lead echo bird sweep harm ring bowl knock bass shatter chimes

voice lead     crystal    vol=0.8  pan=0.1
voice echo     crystal    vol=0.28 pan=-0.4 rev=0.7
voice bird     crystal    vol=0.5  pan=0.4  rev=0.75
voice sweep    crystal    vol=0.28 pan=0.35 rev=0.6
voice harm     glassharp  vol=0.3  pan=-0.2 center=A4 att=0.15 rel=1.2
voice ring     glassharp  vol=0.2  pan=0.3  rev=0.8 att=0.1 rel=1
voice bowl     bowl       vol=0.55 pan=-0.1
voice knock    kick       vol=0.4
voice bass     fretless   vol=0.6
voice shatter  shatter    vol=0.5  pan=0.15
voice chimes   chimes     vol=0.45 pan=-0.3

# the blow, a ring while time stands still, the shatter, and the toy tune rising out of it: (D) | F G
pattern strike
knock   | X..... ...... | _ |
bass    | D1!- .--------- | F1----- G1----- |
ring    | G6----------- | -- .--------- |
shatter | _ | X..... ...... |
chimes  | _ | x..x.. ...... |
lead    | _ | A5- B5- C6- E6--- D6- |
echo    | _ | . A5- B5- C6- E6--- D6 |
harm    | _ | [F]----- [G]----- |

# it lands on A major, broadening: the tune's C as C#, a sweep, the bowl and the bird's wide call
pattern land tempo=80
lead    | C#6!----------- |
echo    | - C#6---------- |
bird    | .--- E7 A6+B6------ |
sweep   | A4 C#5 E5 A5 C#6 E6 A6----- |
harm    | [A]!----------- |
bowl    | A2!----------- |
bass    | A1----------- |

loop strike land
